==================== Instruction ====================
I want a technical specifications knowledge base where engineers can browse technical documents organized by modules. Each document should display its title, content sections, and any related documents it references. Users should be able to navigate between related documents through clickable links and collapse or expand content sections to make reading easier.An additional advanced function is dynamic knowledge graph visualization for document relationships, which visually maps connections between modules, documents and key knowledge points with interactive nodes and links for intuitive navigation.It is divided into the tabs of Document View, Graph and Favorites; the previously adjusted page states (e.g., whether paragraphs are collapsed or expanded, the zoom level of the graph) must be retained when switching tabs. Paragraphs must be expanded before their links can be clicked, and the page shall display a prompt if a link is clicked prematurely. Document information shall be displayed synchronously across different tabs. Favorite content is stored locally, with a real-time count of favorites maintained; favorite markers shall not be lost after filtering and sorting. The page must show corresponding prompts for scenarios such as no documents found and invalid links.
