ase-schema set its state to \\\"selected\\\" (and cleared the prior node), rendering a glow ring (circle r=28, class animate-pulse-glow) plus thicker stroke. Zoom In ×2: graph.zoom 100%→120%→140%; Zoom Out →120% with root transform scale(1.2); Reset View → 100% and translate(0, 0) scale(1).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Graph renders 19 nodes (all documents across API/AUTH/DATA/UI/CORE) and 19 edge lines matching all unique related-document pairs. At 100% one node overflowed the canvas bottom; Zoom Out to 80% (scale(0.8)) placed all 19/19 nodes fully within the canvas.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"nav.documents, nav.graph and nav.favorites all present; clicked through Documents→Graph→Documents→Graph→Favorites, each time the clicked tab became state=\\\"active\\\" and rendered its view (library.list / graph.nodes / favorites.list with empty message \\\"No favorites yet\\\").\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Set doc=Data Migrations with migration-workflow=closed / zero-downtime=open and graph zoom=90%. Documents→Favorites→Documents→Graph round trip: doc.title stayed \\\"Data Migrations\\\", section states stayed closed/open in both Documents and Favorites views, graph returned at zoom 90% (scale(0.9)) with node data-migrations still selected. Caveat: pan state stayed translate(0,0) throughout because canvas panning never responds (real Playwright drag on the canvas background and separate-task mousedown/mousemove/mouseup both left translate unchanged, while wheel-zoom on the same canvas did work), so a non-default pan value could not be produced to test.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Documents module filter leaks into the Favorites view, hiding favorited documents from other modules\", \"actual\": \"With 3 favorites (rest-api-design/API, jwt-authentication/AUTH, design-tokens/UI), selecting the UI module filter in Documents and then opening Favorites showed only favorites.list.item.design-tokens — jwt-authentication and rest-api-design were absent — even though nav.favorites.count still read 3 and the Favorites view exposes no module filter control of its own to clear. Resetting Documents to \\\"All\\\" restored all 3 entries in Favorites, confirming the Documents filter drives the Favorites list.\", \"evidence\": \"Other FT-10 clauses passed: count updated immediately (0→\\\"Favorites 1\\\"→3), markers survived sort by Last Updated (all 3 still state=on) and survived module filtering (design-tokens state=on under UI filter), and after a page reload localStorage key tech-docs-storage retained favorites [\\\"jwt-authentication\\\",\\\"design-tokens\\\",\\\"rest-api-design\\\"] with count 3 and all 3 stars still on.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Visited all 19 documents and collected related-doc ids and section reference-link ids for each; zero self-references found in either location (selfRefs=[]). 34 related-document edges total.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Graph SVG contains 19 g.graph-node elements — one per available document — and 19 edge <line> elements, exactly matching the 19 unique undirected related-document pairs derived from all documents' related lists. Node circles are stroked per module (API=hsl(187,85%,53%), AUTH=hsl(271,81%,56%), DATA=hsl(142,71%,45%), UI=hsl(38,92%,50%), CORE=hsl(346,77%,50%)).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Each section header carries a chevron-down icon; closed section rest-principles has class \\\"...transition-transform\\\", open section endpoint-naming adds \\\"rotate-180\\\". Indicator state matches data-semtag-state and the visibility of section content/enabled links.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-16\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Graph node click does not open the document view; a manual tab switch is required\", \"actual\": \"Single-clicking node graph.nodes.item.database-schema (and double-clicking graph.nodes.item.data-migrations) only marked the node state=\\\"selected\\\". The active tab remained nav.graph, no doc.title element existed anywhere in the DOM, and no document panel/preview appeared in the graph view. Only after manually clicking nav.documents did the document open (doc.title=\\\"Data Migrations\\\"), showing selection does sync but the node click alone never opens the document view.\", \"evidence\": \"After node click: activeTab=[\\\"nav.graph\\\"], docTitlePresent=false, graphPresent=true. Graph view itself is preserved for later return.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Collapsed section 'endpoint-naming' link http-methods: click kept doc.title=\\\"REST API Design Guidelines\\\" and rendered toast \\\"Please expand the section to access links\\\". After expanding the section the link name changed from \\\"Expand section to access link\\\" (disabled) to \\\"HTTP Methods Guide\\\"; clicking it set doc.title=\\\"HTTP Methods Guide\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Search \\\"zzzznotfound\\\" → 0 items and library.list.empty shows \\\"No documents found / Try adjusting your search or filter criteria\\\". Combination search \\\"jwt\\\" + UI module (no overlap) → same no-results message, 0 items. Clearing the search restored the 3 UI documents (accessibility-standards, component-library, design-tokens) with the empty message gone.\"}]}"
